Both forms of the nudge ended "the undeclared-state class is WI-nazoj".
That item is closed: its ten undeclared exits now declare their state, and
an abort the ERR trap can see records the line it died on. A reader
following that pointer lands on finished work instead of on the evidence.

They route to the abort site instead, and the markdown form says what a
MISSING site means — a `set -u` unbound variable and a bare `exit` never
reach the ERR trap, so "not recorded" is the signal to go looking by hand
rather than an absence of failure.

A nudge is a router. Pointing it at a closed item is the WI-lapap defect
one hop along: not an instrument with no reader, but a reader sent
somewhere there is nothing left to read.

